# 2️⃣ Left Rotate Array by K Positions

## 📖 Definition

Rotate the array left by K positions.

---

### Example

Before

```text
1 2 3 4 5 6 7
```

Rotate by K = 2

After

```text
3 4 5 6 7 1 2
```

---

### Best Approach

Use the **Reversal Algorithm**.

Steps

```
Reverse first K elements

Reverse remaining elements

Reverse complete array
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

### Space Complexity

```
O(1)
```

---

# 3️⃣ Right Rotate Array by One Position

## 📖 Definition

Every element shifts one position towards the right.

The last element moves to the first position.

---

### Example

Before

```text
1 2 3 4 5
```

After

```text
5 1 2 3 4
```

---

### Algorithm

```
Store last element

Shift remaining elements right

Place last element at index 0
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

### Space Complexity

```
O(1)
```

---

# 4️⃣ Move All Zeros to End

## 📖 Definition

Move every zero to the end while maintaining the relative order of non-zero elements.

---

### Example

Before

```text
0 1 0 3 12
```

After

```text
1 3 12 0 0
```

---

### Best Approach

Use the **Two Pointer Technique**.

One pointer tracks the next non-zero position.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
void moveZeros(int arr[], int n)
{
    int j = 0;

    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
    {
        if(arr[i]!=0)
        {
            swap(arr[i],arr[j]);
            j++;
        }
    }
}
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

### Space Complexity

```
O(1)
```

