# 5️⃣ Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array

## 📖 Definition

Given a sorted array, remove duplicate elements without using extra space.

---

### Example

Before

```text
1 1 2 2 3 4 4 5
```

After

```text
1 2 3 4 5
```

---

### Best Approach

Use the **Two Pointer Technique**.

---

### Algorithm

```
Initialize i = 0

Traverse using j

If arr[i] != arr[j]

Increment i

Copy arr[j]
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
int removeDuplicates(int arr[], int n)
{
    int i = 0;

    for(int j=1;j<n;j++)
    {
        if(arr[i]!=arr[j])
        {
            i++;
            arr[i]=arr[j];
        }
    }

    return i+1;
}
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

### Space Complexity

```
O(1)
```

